{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Have I yet sons.</b> Many of our companions thought that this answer is directed against the deniers, but they did not know that our ancestors transmitted that yibbum applies to brothers from the father's side, not from the mother's side. She only said to them: if I had sons in my womb I would give them to you in place of the dead — and this is a way of endearment, not by way of yibbum."], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:18.463159497Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}